 "notes": "The wide sandy bay of Marsa Abu Dabab: the beach entry, the north reef with its ergs, the south reef, and the seagrass meadow in 10-12 m where green turtles graze and dugongs are occasionally seen. Coastline and reef flats from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL); the ergs, turtle and dugong areas, the marker buoy and depths are schematic and not to scale. Parts of the meadow are closed to divers under the protected-area rules; the route is a typical beach dive, not a signed trail, and all positions are approximate.",
